A||||3||cowans||Help! V8 shift cables?||||1||
Z||000000||cowans||10-30-2000||03:19 PM||||I asked this before and thought I'd found the answer.... What have V8 people used for shift cables on a stretched chassis/(4 speed). I tried using 2 getrag(longer) select cables but unfortunately the "SHIFT throw" is not long enough.("SELECT throw" is fine) I know someone suggested earlier to use a marine cable...I may go that route just because marine cables come with adjustments built in!!! Any other thoughts? Anyone tried dismantling select cables to gain (throw)distance? thanks, Sandy||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodney||10-30-2000||03:41 PM||||On my Getrag I made the shift lever on the trans shorter making the throw shorter.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Archie||10-30-2000||07:34 PM||||Depends on the length of the stretch..... <P>I've always managed to use the stock cables. You can use the stck 4 speed cables if you siamese the 2 holes thru the bulkhead into a slot and allow the cables to go thru the bulkhead as clost to the left side of the car as you can. I've used this method on several T.R.'s which have a 7.25" stretch.<P>Archie ||||reg||1
Z||000003||cowans||10-31-2000||11:03 AM||||Thanks Rodney, Archie. Will give both suggestions a try. Sandy||||reg||1
